.TH ALIEN-THUNDER 1 "September 2026" "alien-thunder" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
alien-thunder \- keyboard lighting, G-Mode and sensor readouts for Alienware laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alien-thunder
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a command,
.B alien-thunder
opens the lighting editor: per-key keyboard colors, the touchpad, the alien head and
the power button, saved as profiles. A user service keeps the active profile applied,
turns G-Mode on and off with Fn+F1, and publishes CPU and GPU temperature, fan speeds,
CPU load, GPU memory and RAM for the KDE Plasma panel widget and the overlay.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List the profiles; the active one is marked with *.
.TP
.BI set " profile"
Make a profile the active one and apply it.
.TP
.BR apply " [\fIprofile\fR]"
Apply a profile now (the active one by default) without changing the active one.
.TP
.B status
Show the service and the lighting devices.
.TP
.BR power " [\fIprofile\fR]"
Write the power button colors now.
.TP
.BR gmode " [\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBtoggle\fR]"
Switch G-Mode, the same as Fn+F1; without an argument, show whether it is on.
.TP
.BR overlay " [\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBshow\fR \fIitem\fR|\fBhide\fR \fIitem\fR|\fBitems\fR \fIitem,...\fR|\fBstatus\fR]"
Control the bar of readouts that floats above other windows. Items are cpu_temp,
cpu_load, gpu_temp, gpu_mem, cpu_fan, gpu_fan, ram, ram_gb, download and upload.
Network gauges use a ten-second moving average.
Use "overlay style analog" or "overlay style digital" to select the display,
and "overlay size 50" through "overlay size 250" to set its size in percent.
.TP
.BR desktop " [\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBstatus\fR]"
Control the horizontal desktop gauge bar. Its widget settings select the readings
and analog or digital style independently of the overlay.
.TP
.BR network " [\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBstatus\fR]"
Control the optional per-application network widget on the desktop.
.TP
.BR import-windows " [\fB\-\-list\fR | \fB\-\-id\fR \fIid\fR ...]"
Import Alienware Command Center presets from a Windows partition mounted at /mnt/windows.
.TP
.B setup
Per-user setup after installing a package: turns the service on, puts the widget on
the panel, and reports a missing udev rule or input group.
.TP
.B daemon
The service itself, started by systemd \-\-user.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/alien-thunder/
Profiles, settings and the overlay position.
.SH NOTES
Fn+F1 needs the user in the
.B input
group. G-Mode relies on the kernel alienware-wmi driver and power-profiles-daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/cryptoconspiracy/alien-thunder
